    },
    {
      "id": "t-96433126",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 928,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 22.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#5f3dc4",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 599074721,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2110634423,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Two tiers, three axes: provenance (keep originals) · retrievability · canonicalization.\n• Human-in-the-loop approval gates the knowledge corpus.\n• Agentic judgment keeps personal/contradicted notes out of canonical knowledge.\n• Mechanical chunk boundaries; LLM spent on per-chunk context (Anthropic-style), not segmentation.\n• Hybrid retrieval: concept graph = global recall @ note; vector + context = local precision @ chunk;\n  BM25 = lexical. Fused with RRF.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• Two tiers, three axes: provenance (keep originals) · retrievability · canonicalization.\n• Human-in-the-loop approval gates the knowledge corpus.\n• Agentic judgment keeps personal/contradicted notes out of canonical knowledge.\n• Mechanical chunk boundaries; LLM spent on per-chunk context (Anthropic-style), not segmentation.\n• Hybrid retrieval: concept graph = global recall @ note; vector + context = local precision @ chunk;\n  BM25 = lexical. Fused with RRF.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 15
    }
  ],
  "appState": {
    "gridSize": null,
    "viewBackgroundColor": "#ffffff"
  },
